{
  "title": "20: Taa-Haa طه",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nطٰهٰ‌ ۚ‏(1)\nTAAHAA.\nTa-Ha. \nمَاۤ اَنْزَلْنَا عَلَيْكَ الْقُرْاٰنَ لِتَشْقٰٓى ۙ‏(2)\nMAA ANZALNAA A’LAYKA QURAANA LETASHQAAA.\nWe have not sent down the Qur'an to thee to be (an occasion) for thy distress, \nاِلَّا تَذْكِرَةً لِّمَنْ يَّخْشٰى ۙ‏(3)\nILLAA TAZKERATANW LEMAN YAKHSHAA.\nBut only as an admonition to those who fear (Allah), \nتَنْزِيْلًا مِّمَّنْ خَلَقَ الْاَرْضَ وَالسَّمٰوٰتِ الْعُلَى ؕ‏(4)\nTANZEELAA MIMMAYN KHALAQAL ARZA WA SAMAAWAATE AL-U’ULAA.\nA revelation from Him Who created the earth and the heavens on high. \nاَلرَّحْمٰنُ عَلَى الْعَرْشِ اسْتَوٰى‏(5)\nAR-RAHMAAN A’LAL A’RSHIL TAWAA.\n(Allah) Most Gracious is firmly established on the throne (of authority). \nلَهٗ مَا فِى السَّمٰوٰتِ وَمَا فِى الْاَرْضِ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا وَمَا تَحْتَ الثَّرٰى‏(6)\nLAHU MAA FIL SAMAAWAATE WA MAA FIL ARZE WA MAA BAYNAHOMAA WA MAA TAHTA AS-SARAA.\nTo Him belongs what is in the heavens and on earth, and all between them, and all beneath the soil. \nوَاِنْ تَجْهَرْ بِالْقَوْلِ فَاِنَّهٗ يَعْلَمُ السِّرَّ وَاَخْفٰى‏(7)\nWA TAJHAR BIL-QAWLE FA-INNAHU YA’LAMO AS-SERRA WAAKHFAA.\nIf thou pronounce the word aloud, (it is no matter): for verily He knoweth what is secret and what is yet more hidden. \nاَللّٰهُ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ ‌ؕ لَهُ الْاَسْمَآءُ الْحُسْنٰى‏(8)\nALLAAHO LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOWA LAHUL ASMAA-UL AL-HUSNAA.\nAllah! there is no god but He! To Him belong the most Beautiful Names. \n‌وَهَلْ اَتٰٮكَ حَدِيْثُ مُوْسٰى‌ۘ‏(9)\nWA HAL ATAAKA HADEESUL MOOSAA.\nHas the story of Moses reached thee? \nاِذْ رَاٰ نَارًا فَقَالَ لِاَهْلِهِ امْكُثُوْۤا اِنِّىْۤ اٰنَسْتُ نَارًا لَّعَلِّىْۤ اٰتِيْكُمْ مِّنْهَا بِقَبَسٍ اَوْ اَجِدُ عَلَى النَّارِ هُدًى‏(10)\nIZ RAA NAARAN FAQAALA LE-AHLEHIM KOSOO INNEE AANASTO NAARAN LA-A’LLEE AATEEKUM MINHAA BE-QABASIL AW AAJEDU A’LAL NAAR HODAM.\nBehold, he saw a fire: So he said to his family, “Tarry ye; I perceive a fire; perhaps I can bring you some burning brand therefrom, or find some guidance at the fire.” \nفَلَمَّاۤ اَتٰٮهَا نُوْدِىَ يٰمُوْسٰىؕ‏(11)\nFALAMMAA ATAAHAA NOODEYA YAAMOOSAA.\nBut when he came to the fire, a voice was heard: “O Moses! \nاِنِّىْۤ اَنَا رَبُّكَ فَاخْلَعْ نَعْلَيْكَ‌ۚ اِنَّكَ بِالْوَادِ الْمُقَدَّسِ طُوًىؕ‏(12)\nINNEE ANAA RABBOKA FAAKHLAA’ NAA’LAYKA INNAKA BIL-WAADE AL-MUQADDASE TOOAA.\n“Verily I am thy Lord! therefore (in My presence) put off thy shoes: thou art in the sacred valley Tuwa. \nوَاَنَا اخْتَرْتُكَ فَاسْتَمِعْ لِمَا يُوْحٰى‏(13)\nANAT AKHTARTUKA FAASTAMEA’ LEMAKH YOOHAA.\n“I have chosen thee: listen, then, to the inspiration (sent to thee). \nاِنَّنِىْۤ اَنَا اللّٰهُ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّاۤ اَنَا فَاعْبُدْنِىْ ۙ وَاَقِمِ الصَّلٰوةَ لِذِكْرِىْ‏(14)\nINNANEE ANAA LAAHO LAA ELAAHA ILLAA ANAA FAAA’BUDNEAA WA SALAATA LEZEKREAA.\n“Verily, I am Allah: There is no god but I: So serve thou Me (only), and establish regular prayer for celebrating My praise. \nاِنَّ السَّاعَةَ اٰتِيَةٌ اَكَادُ اُخْفِيْهَا لِتُجْزٰى كُلُّ نَفْسٍۢ بِمَا تَسْعٰى‏(15)\nINNAL SAA-A’TA AAATEETUN AAKAADU AUKHFEEHAA LETUJZAA KULLO NAFSIM BEMAA TASA’AA.\n“Verily the Hour is coming - My design is to keep it hidden - for every soul to receive its reward by the measure of its Endeavour. \nفَلَا يَصُدَّنَّكَ عَنْهَا مَنْ لَّا يُؤْمِنُ بِهَا وَاتَّبَعَ هَوٰٮهُ فَتَرْدٰى‏(16)\nFALAA YASUDDANNAKA A’NHAA MAN LAA BIL LAAHE BEHAA WA TABA-A’L HAWHU FATARDAA.\n“Therefore let not such as believe not therein but follow their own lusts, divert thee therefrom, lest thou perish!”.. \nوَمَا تِلْكَ بِيَمِيْنِكَ يٰمُوْسٰى‏(17)\nWA MAA TILKA BE-YAMEENEKA YAA MOOSAA.\n“And what is that in the right hand, O Moses?” \nقَالَ هِىَ عَصَاىَ‌ۚ اَتَوَكَّؤُا عَلَيْهَا وَاَهُشُّ بِهَا عَلٰى غَنَمِىْ وَلِىَ فِيْهَا مَاٰرِبُ اُخْرٰى‏(18)\nQAALA HEYA A’ASAAAAA AATAWAKKAUA A’LAYHAA WAAHUSSHU BEHAA A’LAA GHANAMEAA WA LEYA FEEHAA MAAREBU LAHU.\nHe said, “It is my rod: on it I lean; with it I beat down fodder for my flocks; and in it I find other uses.” \nقَالَ اَلْقِهَا يٰمُوْسٰى‏(19)\nQAALA AALQEHAA YAA MOOSAA.\n(Allah) said, “Throw it, O Moses!” \nفَاَلْقٰٮهَا فَاِذَا هِىَ حَيَّةٌ تَسْعٰى‏(20)\nFAALQAAHAA FA-EZAA HEYA HAYTUN TASA’AA.\nHe threw it, and behold! It was a snake, active in motion. \nقَالَ خُذْهَا وَلَا تَخَفْ‌ سَنُعِيْدُهَا سِيْرَتَهَا الْاُوْلٰى‏(21)\nQAALA KHUZHAA WA LAA TAKHAF SANUE’EEDUHAA SEERATAHAA OOLAA.\n(Allah) said, “Seize it, and fear not: We shall return it at once to its former condition”.. \nوَاضْمُمْ يَدَكَ اِلٰى جَنَاحِكَ تَخْرُجْ بَيْضَآءَ مِنْ غَيْرِ سُوْٓءٍ اٰيَةً اُخْرٰىۙ‏(22)\nWAAZMUM YADAKA ELAA JANAAHEKA TAKHRUJ BAYZAAA-A MIN GHAIRE SOOO-IN AAYATAL LAHU.\n“Now draw thy hand close to thy side: It shall come forth white (and shining), without harm (or stain), as another Sign, \nلِنُرِيَكَ مِنْ اٰيٰتِنَا الْكُبْرٰى‌ۚ‏(23)\nLENUREEKA MIN AAYAATENAA KUBRAA.\n“In order that We may show thee (two) of our Greater Signs. \nاِذْهَبْ اِلٰى فِرْعَوْنَ اِنَّهٗ طَغٰى‏(24)\nIZHAB ELAA FIR-A’WNA INNAHU TAGHAA.\n“Go thou to Pharaoh, for he has indeed transgressed all bounds.” \nقَالَ رَبِّ اشْرَحْ لِىْ صَدْرِىْ ۙ‏(25)\nQAALA RABBE ASHRAH LEE SADREAA.\n(Moses) said: “O my Lord! expand me my breast; \nوَيَسِّرْ لِىْۤ اَمْرِىْ ۙ‏(26)\nWAYASSER LEE AMREE.\n“Ease my task for me; \nوَاحْلُلْ عُقْدَةً مِّنْ لِّسَانِیْ ۙ‏(27)\nWAAHLUL U’UQDATAN MIN LLESAANEE.\n“And remove the impediment from my speech, \nيَفْقَهُوْا قَوْلِیْ ‏(28)\nYAFQAHOOA QAWLEE.\n“So they may understand what I say: \nوَاجْعَلْ لِّىْ وَزِيْرًا مِّنْ اَهْلِىْ ۙ‏(29)\nWA A’L LEE WAZEERAN MIN AAHLEAA.\n“And give me a Minister from my family, \nهٰرُوْنَ اَخِى ۙ‏(30)\nAALO AAKHEAA.\n“Aaron, my brother; \nاشْدُدْ بِهٖۤ اَزْرِىْ ۙ‏(31)\nASHDUD BEHI AAZREAA.\n“Add to my strength through him, \nوَاَشْرِكْهُ فِىْۤ اَمْرِىْ ۙ‏(32)\nWAASHREKHU FEE AMREE.\n“And make him share my task: \nكَىْ نُسَبِّحَكَ كَثِيْرًا ۙ‏(33)\nKAY NUSABBEHAKA KASEERAA.\n“That we may celebrate Thy praise without stint, \nوَّنَذْكُرَكَ كَثِيْرًا ؕ‏(34)\nWWANAZKURAKA KASEERAA.\n“And remember Thee without stint: \nاِنَّكَ كُنْتَ بِنَا بَصِيْرًا‏(35)\nINNAKA KUNTA LAKHASAFA BASEERAA.\n“For Thou art He that (ever) regardeth us.” \nقَالَ قَدْ اُوْتِيْتَ سُؤْلَكَ يٰمُوْسٰى‏(36)\nQAALA QAD AOOTEETA SULAKA YAA MOOSAA.\n(Allah) said: “Granted is thy prayer, O Moses!” \nوَلَقَدْ مَنَنَّا عَلَيْكَ مَرَّةً اُخْرٰٓىۙ‏(37)\nWA LAQAD MANANNAA A’LAYKA MARRATAN AUKHRAAA.\n“And indeed We conferred a favour on thee another time (before). \nاِذْ اَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلٰٓى اُمِّكَ مَا يُوْحٰٓى ۙ‏(38)\nIZ AAWHAYNAA ELAA AUMMEKA MAA YOOHAA.\n“Behold! We sent to thy mother, by inspiration, the message: \nاَنِ اقْذِفِيْهِ فِى التَّابُوْتِ فَاقْذِفِيْهِ فِى الْيَمِّ فَلْيُلْقِهِ الْيَمُّ بِالسَّاحِلِ يَاْخُذْهُ عَدُوٌّ لِّىْ وَعَدُوٌّ لَّهٗ‌ ؕ وَاَلْقَيْتُ عَلَيْكَ مَحَبَّةً مِّنِّىْ ۚ وَلِتُصْنَعَ عَلٰى عَيْنِىْ ۘ‏(39)\nSAALEHAN AQZEFEEHE FIL AT-TAABOOTE FAAQZEFEEHE FIL WA FALYULQEHE AL-YAMMU BEALSSAAHELE YAAKHUZHU A’DUWWUM LEE WA A’DUWWUM LAHU WAALQAYTU A’LAYKA MAHABBATAN MINNEE WALETUSNAA’A A’LAA A’AYNEAA.\n“'Throw (the child) into the chest, and throw (the chest) into the river: the river will cast him up on the bank, and he will be taken up by one who is an enemy to Me and an enemy to him': But I cast (the garment of) love over thee from Me: and (this) in order that thou mayest be reared under Mine eye. \nاِذْ تَمْشِىْۤ اُخْتُكَ فَتَقُوْلُ هَلْ اَدُلُّكُمْ عَلٰى مَنْ يَّكْفُلُهٗ‌ ؕ فَرَجَعْنٰكَ اِلٰٓى اُمِّكَ كَىْ تَقَرَّ عَيْنُهَا وَلَا تَحْزَنَ ؕ وَقَتَلْتَ نَفْسًا فَنَجَّيْنٰكَ مِنَ الْغَمِّ وَفَتَنّٰكَ فُتُوْنًا فَلَبِثْتَ سِنِيْنَ فِىْۤ اَهْلِ مَدْيَنَ ۙ ثُمَّ جِئْتَ عَلٰى قَدَرٍ يّٰمُوْسٰى‏(40)\nIZ TAMSHEE AUKHTUKA FA TAQOOLO HAL ADULLOKUM A’LAA MAN YYAKFULUH FARAJAA’NAAKA ELAA AUMMEKA KAY TAQARRA A’YNOHAA WA LAA TAHZANA WA NAFSAM NAFSAN FANAJJAYNAAKA MENAL AL-GHAMME WAFATANNAAKA FUTOONAN FALABESTA SENEEN FEE AHLIL MADYANA SUMMA BIL-HAQ A’LAA QADARIN YYAAMOOSAA.\n“Behold! thy sister goeth forth and saith, 'shall I show you one who will nurse and rear the (child)?' So We brought thee back to thy mother, that her eye might be cooled and she should not grieve. Then thou didst slay a man, but We saved thee from trouble, and We tried thee in various ways. Then didst thou tarry a number of years with the people of Midian. Then didst thou come hither as ordained, O Moses! \nوَاصْطَنَعْتُكَ لِنَفْسِى‌ۚ‏(41)\nWAASTANAA’TUKA LENAFSEAA.\n“And I have prepared thee for Myself (for service)”.. \nاِذْهَبْ اَنْتَ وَاَخُوْكَ بِاٰيٰتِىْ وَلَا تَنِيَا فِىْ ذِكْرِى‌ۚ‏(42)\nIZHAB ANTA WAAKHOOKA BE-AAYAATEE WA LAA TANEEA FEE ZEKREAA.\n“Go, thou and thy brother, with My Signs, and slacken not, either of you, in keeping Me in remembrance. \nاِذْهَبَاۤ اِلٰى فِرْعَوْنَ اِنَّهٗ طَغٰى‌ ‌ۖۚ‌‌‌‏(43)\nAEZHABAA ELAA FIR-A’WNA INNAHU TAGHAA.\n“Go, both of you, to Pharaoh, for he has indeed transgressed all bounds; \nفَقُوْلَا لَهٗ قَوْلًا لَّيِّنًا لَّعَلَّهٗ يَتَذَكَّرُ اَوْ يَخْشٰى‏(44)\nFAQOOLAA LAHU QAWLAM LLAYNAN LLAA’ALLAH YATAZAKKARU AW YAKHSHAA.\n“But speak to him mildly; perchance he may take warning or fear (Allah).” \nقَالَا رَبَّنَاۤ اِنَّنَا نَخَافُ اَنْ يَّفْرُطَ عَلَيْنَاۤ اَوْ اَنْ يَّطْغٰى‏(45)\nQAALAA RABBANAA INNANAA NAKHAAFO AN YYAFRUTA A’LAYNAA AW AN YYATGHAA.\nThey (Moses and Aaron) said: “Our Lord! We fear lest he hasten with insolence against us, or lest he transgress all bounds.” \nقَالَ لَا تَخَافَآ‌ اِنَّنِىْ مَعَكُمَاۤ اَسْمَعُ وَاَرٰى‏(46)\nQAALA LAA TAKHAAFAA INNANEE MAA’AKUMAA AASMAU’U WAARAA.\nHe said: “Fear not: for I am with you: I hear and see (everything). \nفَاْتِيٰهُ فَقُوْلَاۤ اِنَّا رَسُوْلَا رَبِّكَ فَاَرْسِلْ مَعَنَا بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ ۙ وَلَا تُعَذِّبْهُمْ‌ ؕ قَدْ جِئْنٰكَ بِاٰيَةٍ مِّنْ رَّبِّكَ‌ ؕ وَالسَّلٰمُ عَلٰى مَنِ اتَّبَعَ الْهُدٰى‏(47)\nFAATEEHU FAQOOLAA INNAA RASOOLAA RABBEKA FAARSEL MAA’ANAA BANEE ISRAAA-EELAZ WA LAA TUA’AZZEBHUM QAD JENAAKA BE-AAYATIL MIN RABBEKA WA SALAAMUL A’LAA MANIS TABA-A’L HODAA.\n“So go ye both to him, and say, 'Verily we are messengers sent by thy Lord: Send forth, therefore, the Children of Israel with us, and afflict them not: with a Sign, indeed, have we come from thy Lord! and peace to all who follow guidance! \nاِنَّا قَدْ اُوْحِىَ اِلَيْنَاۤ اَنَّ الْعَذَابَ عَلٰى مَنْ كَذَّبَ وَتَوَلّٰى‏(48)\nINNAA QAD OOHEYA ELAYNAA ANNAL A’ZAABA A’LAA MAN KAZZABA WA TAWALLAA.\n“'Verily it has been revealed to us that the Penalty (awaits) those who reject and turn away.'“ \nقَالَ فَمَنْ رَّبُّكُمَا يٰمُوْسٰى‏(49)\nQAALA FAMAN RRABBUKUMAA YAA MOOSAA.\n(When this message was delivered), (Pharaoh) said: “Who, then, O Moses, is the Lord of you two?” \nقَالَ رَبُّنَا الَّذِىْۤ اَعْطٰى كُلَّ شَىْءٍ خَلْقَهٗ ثُمَّ هَدٰى‏(50)\nQAALA RABBONAA LAZEE A-A’TAA KULLA SHAY-IN KHALQAH SUMMA HADAA.\nHe said: “Our Lord is He Who gave to each (created) thing its form and nature, and further, gave (it) guidance.” \nقَالَ فَمَا بَالُ الْقُرُوْنِ الْاُوْلٰى‏(51)\nQAALA FAMAA BAALU QOROONE OOLAA.\n(Pharaoh) said: “What then is the condition of previous generations?” \nقَالَ عِلْمُهَا عِنْدَ رَبِّىْ فِىْ كِتٰبٍ‌‌ۚ لَا يَضِلُّ رَبِّىْ وَلَا يَنْسَى‏(52)\nQAALA I’LMOHAA I’NDAL RABBEE FEE KETAABIM LAA YAZELLU RABBEE WA LAA YANSAA.\nHe replied: “The knowledge of that is with my Lord, duly recorded: my Lord never errs, nor forgets, \nالَّذِىْ جَعَلَ لَكُمُ الْاَرْضَ مَهْدًا وَّسَلَكَ لَكُمْ فِيْهَا سُبُلًا وَّ اَنْزَلَ مِنَ السَّمَآءِ مَآءً ؕ فَاَخْرَجْنَا بِهٖۤ اَزْوَاجًا مِّنْ نَّبَاتٍ شَتّٰى‏(53)\nLAZEE JA-A’LA LAKOMUL ARZA MAHDAN WWASALAKA LAKUM FEEHAA SUBULAN WA ANZALAL MENAL SAMAAA-E MAAA-AN FA AKH-RAJNAA BEHI AZWAAJANW MIN NNABAATIN SHATTAA.\n“He Who has, made for you the earth like a carpet spread out; has enabled you to go about therein by roads (and channels); and has sent down water from the sky.” With it have We produced diverse pairs of plants each separate from the others. \nكُلُوْا وَارْعَوْا اَنْعَامَكُمْ‌ ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّاُولِى النُّهٰى‏(54)\nKOLOO WAARA’AWA AANA’AAMAKUM INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYAATIL LEAOOLEAA AN-NUHAA.\nEat (for yourselves) and pasture your cattle: verily, in this are Signs for men endued with understanding. \nمِنْهَا خَلَقْنٰكُمْ وَفِيْهَا نُعِيْدُكُمْ وَمِنْهَا نُخْرِجُكُمْ تَارَةً اُخْرٰى‏(55)\nMINHAA KHALAQNAAKUM WA FEEHAA NUE’EEDUKUM WA MINHAA NUKHREJUKUM TAARATAN LAHU.\nFrom the (earth) did We create you, and into it shall We return you, and from it shall We bring you out once again. \nوَلَقَدْ اَرَيْنٰهُ اٰيٰتِنَا كُلَّهَا فَكَذَّبَ وَاَبٰى‏(56)\nWA LAQAD AARAYNAAHU AAYAATENAA KULLAHAA FA KAZZABA WA ABAA.\nAnd We showed Pharaoh all Our Signs, but he did reject and refuse. \nقَالَ اَجِئْتَنَا لِتُخْرِجَنَا مِنْ اَرْضِنَا بِسِحْرِكَ يٰمُوْسٰى‏(57)\nQAALA AAJETANAA LETUKHREJANAA MIN ARZENAA BESEHREKA YAA MOOSAA.\nHe said: “Hast thou come to drive us out of our land with thy magic, O Moses? \nفَلَنَاْتِيَنَّكَ بِسِحْرٍ مِّثْلِهٖ فَاجْعَلْ بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَكَ مَوْعِدًا لَّا نُخْلِفُهٗ نَحْنُ وَلَاۤ اَنْتَ مَكَانًا سُوًى‏(58)\nFALANAATEENNAKA BESEHRIN MISLEH FAJ-A’L BAYNANAA WA WA MAWE’EDAN LAA NUKHLEFUH NAHNO WA LAA ANTA MAKAANAN SOOAA.\n“But we can surely produce magic to match thine! So make a tryst between us and thee, which we shall not fail to keep - neither we nor thou - in a place where both shall have even chances.” \nقَالَ مَوْعِدُكُمْ يَوْمُ الزِّيْنَةِ وَاَنْ يُّحْشَرَ النَّاسُ ضُحًى‏(59)\nQAALA MAWE’EDUKUM YAWMUD AZ-ZEENATE WA YYUHSHARA NAASO ZUHAN.\nMoses said: “Your tryst is the Day of the Festival, and let the people be assembled when the sun is well up.” \nفَتَوَلّٰى فِرْعَوْنُ فَجَمَعَ كَيْدَهٗ ثُمَّ اَتٰى‏(60)\nFA TAWALLAA FIRA’WNO FA JAMA-A’ KAYDAH SUMMA ATAA.\nSo Pharaoh withdrew: He concerted his plan, and then came (back). \nقَالَ لَهُمْ مُّوْسٰى وَيْلَكُمْ لَا تَفْتَرُوْا عَلَى اللّٰهِ كَذِبًا فَيُسْحِتَكُمْ بِعَذَابٍ‌ۚ وَقَدْ خَابَ مَنِ افْتَرٰى‏(61)\nQAALA LAHUM MOOSAA WAYLAKUM LAA TAFTAROOA A’LAL LAAHE KAZEBAN FAYUSHETAKUM BE-A’ZAABIN WA QAD QAD MANIS TARAA.\nMoses said to him: Woe to you! Forge not ye a lie against Allah, lest He destroy you (at once) utterly by chastisement: the forger must suffer frustration!” \nفَتَنَازَعُوْۤا اَمْرَهُمْ بَيْنَهُمْ وَاَسَرُّوا النَّجْوٰى‏(62)\nFATANAAZAU’OOA AAMRAHUM BAYNAHUM WAASARROOA AN-NAJWAA.\nSo they disputed, one with another, over their affair, but they kept their talk secret. \nقَالُوْۤا اِنْ هٰذٰٮنِ لَسٰحِرٰنِ يُرِيْدٰنِ اَنْ يُّخْرِجٰكُمْ مِّنْ اَرْضِكُمْ بِسِحْرِهِمَا وَيَذْهَبَا بِطَرِيْقَتِكُمُ الْمُثْلٰى‏(63)\nQAALOO IN HAAZAANE LASAAHERAANE YUREEDAANE AN YYUKHREJAAKUM MIN AARZEKUM BESEHREHEMAA WAYAZHABAA BETAREEQATEKUMU AL-MUSLAA.\nThey said: “These two are certainly (expert) magicians: their object is to drive you out from your land with their magic, and to do away with your most cherished institutions. \nفَاَجْمِعُوْا كَيْدَكُمْ ثُمَّ ائْتُوْا صَفًّا‌ ۚ وَقَدْ اَفْلَحَ الْيَوْمَ مَنِ اسْتَعْلٰى‏(64)\nFAAJMEU’OOA KAYDAKUM SUMMA ATOOA MALAAA-EKATO WA QAD AFLAHA YAWMA MANIS ASTAA’LAA.\n“Therefore concert your plan, and then assemble in (serried) ranks: He wins (all along) today who gains the upper hand.” \nقَالُوْا يٰمُوْسٰٓى اِمَّاۤ اَنْ تُلْقِىَ وَاِمَّاۤ اَنْ نَّكُوْنَ اَوَّلَ مَنْ اَلْقٰى‏(65)\nQAALOO MOOSAA IMMAA AN TULQEAAA WA AMMAA AN NNAKOONA AWWALA MAN AALQAA.\nThey said: “O Moses! whether wilt thou that thou throw (first) or that we be the first to throw?” \nقَالَ بَلْ اَلْقُوْا‌ۚ فَاِذَا حِبَالُهُمْ وَعِصِيُّهُمْ يُخَيَّلُ اِلَيْهِ مِنْ سِحْرِهِمْ اَنَّهَا تَسْعٰى‏(66)\nQAALA BAL AALQOOA FA-EZAA HEBAALUHUM WAE’ESEEHUM YUKHAYLU ELAYHE MIN SEHREHEM AANNAHAA TASA’AA.\nHe said, “Nay, throw ye first!” Then behold their ropes and their rods-so it seemed to him on account of their magic - began to be in lively motion! \nفَاَوْجَسَ فِىْ نَفْسِهٖ خِيْفَةً مُّوْسٰى‏(67)\nFAAWJASA FEE WA KHEEFATAN MOOSAA.\nSo Moses conceived in his mind a (sort of) fear. \nقُلْنَا لَا تَخَفْ اِنَّكَ اَنْتَ الْاَعْلٰى‏(68)\nQULNAL LAA TAKHAF INNAKA ANTA A-A’LAA.\nWe said: “Fear not! for thou hast indeed the upper hand: \nوَاَ لْقِ مَا فِىْ يَمِيْنِكَ تَلْقَفْ مَا صَنَعُوْا‌ ؕاِنَّمَا صَنَعُوْا كَيْدُ سٰحِرٍ‌ ؕ وَلَا يُفْلِحُ السّٰحِرُ حَيْثُ اَتٰى‏(69)\nWAALQE MAA FEE YAMEENEKA TALQAF MAA SANAU’OOA AENNAMAA SANAU’OOA KAYDU SAAHERIN WA LAA YUFLEHUZ AS-SAAHERU HAYSO ATAA.\n“Throw that which is in thy right hand: Quickly will it swallow up that which they have faked what they have faked is but a magician's trick: and the magician thrives not, (no matter) where he goes.” \nفَاُلْقِىَ السَّحَرَةُ سُجَّدًا قَالُوْۤا اٰمَنَّا بِرَبِّ هٰرُوْنَ وَمُوْسٰى‏(70)\nFA ULQEYA AS-SAHARATU SUJJADANW QAALOO AAMANNAA BE RABBIL AALO WA MOOSAA.\nSo the magicians were thrown down to prostration: they said, “We believe in the Lord of Aaron and Moses”. \nقَالَ اٰمَنْتُمْ لَهٗ قَبْلَ اَنْ اٰذَنَ لَكُمْ‌ؕ اِنَّهٗ لَكَبِيْرُكُمُ الَّذِىْ عَلَّمَكُمُ السِّحْرَ‌ۚ فَلَاُقَطِّعَنَّ اَيْدِيَكُمْ وَاَرْجُلَكُمْ مِّنْ خِلَافٍ وَّلَاُصَلِّبَنَّكُمْ فِىْ جُذُوْعِ النَّخْلِ وَلَتَعْلَمُنَّ اَيُّنَاۤ اَشَدُّ عَذَابًا وَّاَبْقٰى‏(71)\nQAALA AAMANTUM LAHU QABLA AN AAAZANA LAKUM INNAHU LAKABEERUKUMU LAZEE A’ALLAMAKUMU SEHR FALAAQATTEA’ANNA AAYDEEKUM WAARJULAKUM MIN KHELAAFIN WWALAASALLEBANNAKUM FEE JUZOOE’E AN-NAKHLE WALATAA’LAMUNNA AAYNAA ASHADDO A’ZAABAN KHAYRUWN.\n(Pharaoh) said: “Believe ye in Him before I give you permission? Surely this must be your leader, who has taught you magic! be sure I will cut off your hands and feet on opposite sides, and I will have you crucified on trunks of palm-trees: so shall ye know for certain, which of us can give the more severe and the more lasting punishment!” \nقَالُوْا لَنْ نُّؤْثِرَكَ عَلٰى مَا جَآءَنَا مِنَ الْبَيِّنٰتِ وَالَّذِىْ فَطَرَنَا‌ فَاقْضِ مَاۤ اَنْتَ قَاضٍ‌ ؕ اِنَّمَا تَقْضِىْ هٰذِهِ الْحَيٰوةَ الدُّنْيَا ؕ‏(72)\nQAALOO LAN NNUSERAKA A’LAA MAA JAAA-ANAA MENAL BAYYENAATE WAL LAZEE FATARANAA FAAQZE MAA ANTA QAAZIN INNAMAA TAQZEAA HAAZEHE HAYAATAD DUNYAA.\nThey said: “Never shall we regard thee as more than the Clear Signs that have come to us, or than Him Who created us! so decree whatever thou desirest to decree: for thou canst only decree (touching) the life of this world. \nاِنَّاۤ اٰمَنَّا بِرَبِّنَا لِيَغْفِرَ لَنَا خَطٰيٰنَا وَمَاۤ اَكْرَهْتَنَا عَلَيْهِ مِنَ السِّحْرِؕ‌ وَاللّٰهُ خَيْرٌ وَّاَبْقٰى‏(73)\nINNAA AAMANNAA BERABBENAA LEEGHFERA LANAA KHATAAYAANAA WA MAA AAKRAHTANAA A’LAYHE MENAL AS-SEHRE WAL LAAHO KHAYRUL KHAYRUWN.\n“For us, we have believed in our Lord: may He forgive us our faults, and the magic to which thou didst compel us: for Allah is Best and Most Abiding.” \nاِنَّهٗ مَنْ يَّاْتِ رَبَّهٗ مُجْرِمًا فَاِنَّ لَهٗ جَهَنَّمَ‌ۚ لَا يَمُوْتُ فِيْهَا وَ لَا يَحْيٰى‏(74)\nINNAHU MAN INY WAL MUJREMAN FA-INNAL LAHU JAHANNAMA LAA YAMOOTO FEEHAA WA LAA YAHYAA.\nVerily he who comes to his Lord as a sinner (at Judgment), for him is Hell: therein shall he neither die nor live. \nوَمَنْ يَّاْتِهٖ مُؤْمِنًا قَدْ عَمِلَ الصّٰلِحٰتِ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ لَهُمُ الدَّرَجٰتُ الْعُلٰىۙ‏(75)\nWA MAN YYAATEH MUMENAN QAD A’MELA SAALEHAATE FA-OOLAAA-EKA LAHOMUL AD-DARAJAATU AL-U’ULAA.\nBut such as come to Him as Believers who have worked righteous deeds, for them are ranks exalted, \nجَنّٰتُ عَدْنٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَا‌ ؕ وَذٰ لِكَ جَزَآءُ مَنْ تَزَكّٰى‏(76)\nJANNAATU A’ADNIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA WAZAA LEKA JAZAAA-O MAN TAZAKKAA.\nGardens of Eternity, beneath which flow rivers: they will dwell therein for aye: such is the reward of those who purify themselves (from evil). \nوَلَقَدْ اَوْحَيْنَاۤ اِلٰى مُوْسٰٓى ۙ اَنْ اَسْرِ بِعِبَادِىْ فَاضْرِبْ لَهُمْ طَرِيْقًا فِى الْبَحْرِ يَبَسًا ۙ لَّا تَخٰفُ دَرَكًا وَّلَا تَخْشٰى‏(77)\nWA LAQAD AAWHAYNAA ELAA MOOSAA AN AASRE BE-E’BAADEE FAAZREB LAHUM TAREEQAN FIL BAHRE YABASAN LAA TAKHAAFU DARAKAN WA LAA TAKHSHAA.\nWe sent an inspiration to Moses: “Travel by night with My servants, and strike a dry path for them through the sea, without fear of being overtaken (by Pharaoh) and without (any other) fear.” \nفَاَتْبَعَهُمْ فِرْعَوْنُ بِجُنُوْدِهٖ فَغَشِيَهُمْ مِّنَ الْيَمِّ مَا غَشِيَهُمْؕ‏(78)\nFAATBAA’AHUM FIRA’WNO BEJUNOODEH FAGHASHEEHUM MENAL WA MAA GHASHEEHUM.\nThen Pharaoh pursued them with his forces, but the waters completely overwhelmed them and covered them up. \nوَاَضَلَّ فِرْعَوْنُ قَوْمَهٗ وَمَا هَدٰى‏(79)\nWA AZALLAL FIRA’WNO QAWMAH WA MAA HADAA.\nPharaoh led his people astray instead of leading them aright. \nيٰبَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ قَدْ اَنْجَيْنٰكُمْ مِّنْ عَدُوِّكُمْ وَوٰعَدْنٰكُمْ جَانِبَ الطُّوْرِ الْاَيْمَنَ وَنَزَّلْنَا عَلَيْكُمُ الْمَنَّ وَالسَّلْوٰى‏(80)\nYAA BANEE ISRAAA-EELAZ QAD AANJAYNAAKUM MIN A’ADOOKUM WAWA’ADNAAKUM JAANEBA TOORE AL-AAYMANA WA NAZZALNAA A’LAYKOMUL MANNA WAALSSALWAA.\nO ye Children of Israel! We delivered you from your enemy, and We made a Covenant with you on the right side of Mount (Sinai), and We sent down to you Manna and quails: \nكُلُوْا مِنْ طَيِّبٰتِ مَا رَزَقْنٰكُمْ وَلَا تَطْغَوْا فِيْهِ فَيَحِلَّ عَلَيْكُمْ غَضَبِىْ‌ۚ وَمَنْ يَّحْلِلْ عَلَيْهِ غَضَبِىْ فَقَدْ هَوٰى‏(81)\nKOLOO MIN TAYYEBAATE MAA RAZAQNAAKUM WA LAA TATGHAW FEEHE FAYAHELLA A’LAYKUM GHAZABEAA WA MAN YYAHLEL A’LAYHE GHAZABEAA FAQAD HAWAA.\n(Saying): “Eat of the good things We have provided for your sustenance, but commit no excess therein, lest My Wrath should justly descend on you: and those on whom descends My Wrath do perish indeed! \nوَاِنِّىْ لَغَفَّارٌ لِّمَنْ تَابَ وَاٰمَنَ وَعَمِلَ صَالِحًا ثُمَّ اهْتَدٰى‏(82)\nWA INNEE LAGHAFFAARUN LEMAN TAABA WA AAMANA WA A’MELA SAALEHAN SUMMA TADAA.\n“But, without doubt, I am (also) He that forgives again and again, to those who repent, believe, and do right, who, in fine, are ready to receive true guidance.” \nوَمَاۤ اَعْجَلَكَ عَنْ قَوْمِكَ يٰمُوْسٰى‏(83)\nWA MAA AAA’JALAKA A’N QAWMEKA YAA MOOSAA.\n(When Moses was up on the Mount, Allah said:) “What made thee hasten in advance of thy people, O Moses?” \nقَالَ هُمْ اُولَاۤءِ عَلٰٓى اَثَرِىْ وَ عَجِلْتُ اِلَيْكَ رَبِّ لِتَرْضٰى‏(84)\nQAALA HUM AOOLAAE A’LAA AASAREAA WA A’AJELTU ELAYKA RABBE LE-TARZAA.\nHe replied: “Behold, they are close on my footsteps: I hastened to thee, O my Lord, to please thee.” \nقَالَ فَاِنَّا قَدْ فَتَنَّا قَوْمَكَ مِنْۢ بَعْدِكَ وَاَضَلَّهُمُ السَّامِرِىُّ‏(85)\nQAALA FAINNAA QAD FATANNAL QAWMAKA MIN BAA’DEKA WAAZALLAHUMU AS-SAAMEREAAAU.\n(Allah) said: “We have tested thy people in thy absence: the Samiri has led them astray.” \nفَرَجَعَ مُوْسَىٰۤ اِلٰى قَوْمِهٖ غَضْبَانَ اَسِفًا  ۙ قَالَ يٰقَوْمِ اَلَمْ يَعِدْكُمْ رَبُّكُمْ وَعْدًا حَسَنًا  ۙ اَفَطَالَ عَلَيْكُمُ الْعَهْدُ اَمْ اَرَدْتُّمْ اَنْ يَّحِلَّ عَلَيْكُمْ غَضَبٌ مِّنْ رَّبِّكُمْ فَاَخْلَفْتُمْ مَّوْعِدِىْ‏(86)\nFARAJAA’A MOOSAA ELAA QAWMEHI GHAZBAANA AASEFAN QAALA LE-QAWMEHI ALAM YAE’EDKUM RABBOKUM WA’DAN HASANAN AAFATAALA A’LAYKOMUL AL-A’AHDU AM ARAD-TUM AN YYAHELLA A’LAYKUM GHAZABUN MIN RABBEKUM FAAKHLAFTUM MMAWE’EDEAA.\nSo Moses returned to his people in a state of indignation and sorrow. He said: “O my people! did not your Lord make a handsome promise to you? Did then the promise seem to you long (in coming)? Or did ye desire that Wrath should descend from your Lord on you, and so ye broke your promise to me?” \nقَالُوْا مَاۤ اَخْلَفْنَا مَوْعِدَكَ بِمَلْكِنَا وَلٰكِنَّا حُمِّلْنَاۤ اَوْزَارًا مِّنْ زِيْنَةِ الْقَوْمِ فَقَذَفْنٰهَا فَكَذٰلِكَ اَلْقَى السَّامِرِىُّ ۙ‏(87)\nQAALOO MAA AAKHLAFNAA MAWE’EDAKA BEMALKENAA WA LAAKINNAA HUMMELNAA AAWZAARAN MIN ZEENATE QAWMIL FAQAZAFNAAHAA FA KAZAALEKA AALQAA AS-SAAMEREAAAU.\nThey said: “We broke not the promise to thee, as far as lay in our power: but we were made to carry the weight of the ornaments of the (whole) people, and we threw them (into the fire), and that was what the Samiri suggested. \nفَاَخْرَجَ لَهُمْ عِجْلًا جَسَدًا لَّهٗ خُوَارٌ فَقَالُوْا هٰذَاۤ اِلٰهُكُمْ وَاِلٰهُ مُوْسٰى  فَنَسِىَ‏(88)\nFA-AKHRAJA LAHUM E’EJLAN JASADAN LAHU KHOOARUN FA-QAALOO HAAZAA ELAAHOKUM WAALAAHU MOOSAA FANASEAAA.\n“Then he brought out (of the fire) before the (people) the image of a calf: It seemed to low: so they said: This is your god, and the god of Moses, but (Moses) has forgotten!” \nاَفَلَا يَرَوْنَ اَلَّا يَرْجِعُ اِلَيْهِمْ قَوْلًا ۙ وَّلَا يَمْلِكُ لَهُمْ ضَرًّا وَّلَا نَفْعًا‏(89)\nAFALAA YARAWNAL ALLAA YARJE-O’L ELAYHIM QAWLAM WA LAA YAMLEKU LAHUM BEKUM WA LAA BEKUM.\nCould they not see that it could not return them a word (for answer), and that it had no power either to harm them or to do them good? \nوَلَقَدْ قَالَ لَهُمْ هٰرُوْنُ مِنْ قَبْلُ يٰقَوْمِ اِنَّمَا فُتِنْتُمْ بِهٖ‌ۚ وَاِنَّ رَبَّكُمُ الرَّحْمٰنُ فَاتَّبِعُوْنِىْ وَاَطِيْعُوْۤا اَمْرِىْ‏(90)\nWA LAQAD QAALA LAHUM HAAROONO MIN QABLO LE-QAWMEHI INNAMAA FUTENTUM BEHI WA INNA RABBAKOMUL RAHMAANO FAATTABEU’OONEAA WAATEEU’OOA AMREE.\nAaron had already, before this said to them: “O my people! ye are being tested in this: for verily your Lord is (Allah) Most Gracious; so follow me and obey my command.” \nقَالُوْا لَنْ نَّبْرَحَ عَلَيْهِ عٰكِفِيْنَ حَتّٰى يَرْجِعَ اِلَيْنَا مُوْسٰى‏(91)\nQAALOO LAN NNABRAHA A’LAYHE A’AAKEFEENA HATTAA YARJEA’A ELAYNAA MOOSAA.\nThey had said: “We will not abandon this cult, but we will devote ourselves to it until Moses returns to us.” \nقَالَ يٰهٰرُوْنُ مَا مَنَعَكَ اِذْ رَاَيْتَهُمْ ضَلُّوْٓا ۙ‏(92)\nQAALA YAA HAAROONO MAA MANAA’AKA IZ RA-AYTAHUM ZALLOOA.\n(Moses) said: “O Aaron! what kept thee back, when thou sawest them going wrong, \nاَلَّا تَتَّبِعَنِ‌ؕ اَفَعَصَيْتَ اَمْرِىْ‏(93)\nALLAA TATTABEA’ANE AAFAA’ASAYTA AMREE.\n“From following me? Didst thou then disobey my order?” \nقَالَ يَابْنَؤُمَّ لَا تَاْخُذْ بِلِحْيَتِىْ وَلَا بِرَاْسِىْ‌ۚ اِنِّىْ خَشِيْتُ اَنْ تَقُوْلَ فَرَّقْتَ بَيْنَ بَنِىْۤ اِسْرَآءِيْلَ وَلَمْ تَرْقُبْ قَوْلِىْ‏(94)\nQAALA YAABNAUMMA LAA TAAKHUZ BELEHYATEAA WA LAA BERAASEAA INNEE KHASHEETU AN TAQOOLA FARRAQTA BAYNA BANEE ISRAAA-EELAZ WA LAM TARQUB QAWLEAA.\n(Aaron) replied: “O son of my mother! Seize (me) not by my beard nor by (the hair of) my head! Truly I feared lest thou shouldst say, 'Thou has caused a division among the children of Israel, and thou didst not respect my word!'“ \nقَالَ فَمَا خَطْبُكَ يٰسَامِرِىُّ‏(95)\nQAALA FAMAA KHATBUKA YAASAAMEREAAAU.\n(Moses) said: “What then is thy case, O Samiri?” \nقَالَ بَصُرْتُ بِمَا لَمْ يَبْصُرُوْا بِهٖ فَقَبَضْتُ قَبْضَةً مِّنْ اَثَرِ الرَّسُوْلِ فَنَبَذْتُهَا وَكَذٰلِكَ سَوَّلَتْ لِىْ نَفْسِى‏(96)\nQAALA BASURTU BEMAA LAM YABSUROOA BEHI FAQABAZTU QABZATAN MIN WOJOOHEHIM RASOOLE FANABAZTUHAA WA KAZAALEKA SAWLAT LEE NAFSEAA.\nHe replied: “I saw what they saw not: so I took a handful (of dust) from the footprint of the Messenger, and threw it (into the calf): thus did my soul suggest to me.” \nقَالَ فَاذْهَبْ فَاِنَّ لَكَ فِى الْحَيٰوةِ اَنْ تَقُوْلَ لَا مِسَاسَ‌ وَاِنَّ لَكَ مَوْعِدًا لَّنْ تُخْلَفَهٗ‌ ۚ وَانْظُرْ اِلٰٓى اِلٰهِكَ الَّذِىْ ظَلْتَ عَلَيْهِ عَاكِفًا‌ ؕ لَّنُحَرِّقَنَّهٗ ثُمَّ لَنَنْسِفَنَّهٗ فِى الْيَمِّ نَسْفًا‏(97)\nQAALA FAAZHAB FA-INNAL LAKA FIL HAYAATID AN TAQOOLA LAA MESAASA WA INNA LAKA MAWE’EDAN LAN-Y TUKHLAFAH AAYATAL ELAA AELAAHEKA LAZEE ZALTA A’LAYHE A’AAKEFAN LLANUHARREQANNAH SUMMA LANANSEFANNAH FIL WA NASFAN.\n(Moses) said: “Get thee gone! but thy (punishment) in this life will be that thou wilt say, 'touch me not'; and moreover (for a future penalty) thou hast a promise that will not fail: Now look at thy god, of whom thou hast become a devoted worshipper: We will certainly (melt) it in a blazing fire and scatter it broadcast in the sea!” \nاِنَّمَاۤ اِلٰهُكُمُ اللّٰهُ الَّذِىْ لَاۤ اِلٰهَ اِلَّا هُوَ‌ؕ وَسِعَ كُلَّ شَىْءٍ عِلْمًا‏(98)\nINNAMAA AELAAHUKUMU LAAHO LAZEE LAA ELAAHA ILLAA HOO WASEA’ KULLA SHAY-IN I’LMAN.\nBut the god of you all is the One Allah: there is no god but He: all things He comprehends in His knowledge. \nكَذٰلِكَ نَقُصُّ عَلَيْكَ مِنْ اَنْۢبَآءِ مَا قَدْ سَبَقَ‌ ۚ وَقَدْ اٰتَيْنٰكَ مِنْ لَّدُنَّا ذِكْرًا ‌ ۖ‌ ۚ‏(99)\nKAZAALEKA NAQUSSU A’LAYKA MIN AANBAAE MAA QAD SABAQA WA QAD AAATAYNAAKA MIN WA ZIKRAA.\nThus do We relate to thee some stories of what happened before: for We have sent thee a Message from Our own Presence. \nمَنْ اَعْرَضَ عَنْهُ فَاِنَّهٗ يَحْمِلُ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ وِزْرًا ۙ‏(100)\nMAN A-A’RAZA A’NHO FA-INNAHU YAHMELO YAWMA QEYAAMATE WEZRAN.\nIf any do turn away therefrom, verily they will bear a burden on the Day of judgment; \nخٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهِ‌ ؕ وَسَآءَ لَهُمْ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ حِمْلًا ۙ‏(101)\nKHAALEDEENA FEEHE WA SAAA-A LAHUM YAWMA QEYAAMATE HEMLAN.\nThey will abide in this (state): and grievous will the burden be to them on that Day, \nيَّوْمَ يُنْفَخُ فِى الصُّوْرِ‌ وَنَحْشُرُ الْمُجْرِمِيْنَ يَوْمَئِذٍ زُرْقًا‌ ۖ ‌ۚ‏(102)\nYAWMA YUNFAKHO FIL SOORE WA NAHSHORO MUJREMEEN YAWMA-EZIN ZURQAN.\nThe Day when the Trumpet will be sounded: that Day, We shall gather the sinful, blear-eyed (with terror). \nيَّتَخَافَتُوْنَ بَيْنَهُمْ اِنْ لَّبِثْتُمْ اِلَّا عَشْرًا‏(103)\nYYATAKHAAFATOONA BAYNAHUM IN LLABESTUM ILLAA A’SHRAN.\nIn whispers will they consult each other: “Yet tarried not longer than ten (Days); \nنَحْنُ اَعْلَمُ بِمَا يَقُوْلُوْنَ اِذْ يَقُوْلُ اَمْثَلُهُمْ طَرِيْقَةً اِنْ لَّبِثْتُمْ اِلَّا يَوْمًا‏(104)\nNAHNO A-A’LAMO BEMAA YAQOOLOONA IZ YAQOOLO AAMSALUHUM TAREEQATAN IN LLABESTUM ILLAA YAWMAN.\nWe know best what they will say, when their leader most eminent in conduct will say: “Ye tarried not longer than a day!” \nوَيَسْئَلُوْنَكَ عَنِ الْجِبَالِ فَقُلْ يَنْسِفُهَا رَبِّىْ نَسْفًا ۙ‏(105)\nYAS-ALOONAKA A’NIL JEBAALE FAQUL YANSEFUHAA RABBEE NASFAN.\nThey ask thee concerning the Mountains: say, “My Lord will uproot them and scatter them as dust; \nفَيَذَرُهَا قَاعًا صَفْصَفًا ۙ‏(106)\nFAYAZARUHAA QAAA’AN SAFSAFAN.\n“He will leave them as plains smooth and level; \nلَّا تَرٰى فِيْهَا عِوَجًا وَّلَاۤ اَمْتًا ؕ‏(107)\nLAA TARAA FEEHAA E’EWAJAN WA LAA AAMTAN.\n“Nothing crooked or curved wilt thou see in their place.” \nيَوْمَئِذٍ يَّتَّبِعُوْنَ الدَّاعِىَ لَا عِوَجَ لَهٗ‌ؕ وَخَشَعَتِ الْاَصْوَاتُ لِلرَّحْمٰنِ فَلَا تَسْمَعُ اِلَّا هَمْسًا‏(108)\nYAWMA-EZIN YYATTABEU’OONA AD-DAAE’EAAA LAA E’EWAJA LAHU WAKHASHAA’ATE AL-AASWAATU LELRRAHMAANE FALAA TASMAU’U ILLAA HAMSAN.\nOn that Day will they follow the Caller (straight): no crookedness (can they show) him: all sounds shall humble themselves in the Presence of (Allah) Most Gracious: nothing shalt thou hear but the tramp of their feet (as they march). \nيَوْمَئِذٍ لَّا تَنْفَعُ الشَّفَاعَةُ اِلَّا مَنْ اَذِنَ لَهُ الرَّحْمٰنُ وَرَضِىَ لَهٗ قَوْلًا‏(109)\nYAWMA-EZIN LAA TANFAU’U ASH-SHAFAAA’ATU ILLAA MAN AZENA LAHUL RAHMAANO WA RAZEYAL LAHU QAWLAM.\nOn that Day shall no intercession avail except for those for whom permission has been granted by (Allah) Most Gracious and whose word is acceptable to Him. \nيَعْلَمُ مَا بَيْنَ اَيْدِيْهِمْ وَمَا خَلْفَهُمْ وَلَا يُحِيْطُوْنَ بِهٖ عِلْمًا‏(110)\nYA’LAMO MAA BAYNA AYDEEHIM WA MAA KHALFAHUM WA LAA YOHEETOONA BEHI I’LMAN.\nHe knows what (appears to His creatures as) before or after or behind them: but they shall not compass it with their knowledge. \nوَعَنَتِ الْوُجُوْهُ لِلْحَىِّ الْقَيُّوْمِ‌ؕ وَقَدْ خَابَ مَنْ حَمَلَ ظُلْمًا‏(111)\nWAA’ANATE AL-WUJOOHU LIL-HAA AL-QAYWME WA QAD QAD MAN HAMALA ZULMAWN.\n(All) faces shall be humbled before (Him) - the Living, the Self-Subsisting, Eternal: hopeless indeed will be the man that carries iniquity (on his back). \nوَمَنْ يَّعْمَلْ مِنَ الصّٰلِحٰتِ وَهُوَ مُؤْمِنٌ فَلَا يَخٰفُ ظُلْمًا وَّلَا هَضْمًا‏(112)\nWA MAN YA’MAL MENAL SAALEHAATE WA HOWA MUMENUN FALAA YAKHAAFU ZULMAWN WA LAA HAZMAN.\nBut he who works deeds of righteousness, and has faith, will have no fear of harm nor of any curtailment (of what is his due). \nوَكَذٰلِكَ اَنْزَلْنٰهُ قُرْاٰنًا عَرَبِيًّا وَّ صَرَّفْنَا فِيْهِ مِنَ الْوَعِيْدِ لَعَلَّهُمْ يَتَّقُوْنَ اَوْ يُحْدِثُ لَهُمْ ذِكْرًا‏(113)\nWA KAZAALEKA ANZALNAAHO QURAANAN A’RABIYYAL WA SARRAFNAA FEEHE MENAL AL-WAE’EEDE LA-A’LLAHUM YATTAQOON AW LAAHA LAHUM ZIKRAA.\nThus have We sent this down - an arabic Qur'an - and explained therein in detail some of the warnings, in order that they may fear Allah, or that it may cause their remembrance (of Him). \nفَتَعٰلَى اللّٰهُ الْمَلِكُ الْحَقُّ‌ ۚ وَلَا تَعْجَلْ بِالْقُرْاٰنِ مِنْ قَبْلِ اَنْ يُّقْضٰٓى اِلَيْكَ وَحْيُهٗ‌ وَقُلْ رَّبِّ زِدْنِىْ عِلْمًا‏(114)\nFA TA-A’ALAL LAAHO AL-MALEKU HAQQO WA LAA TAA’JAL BE-QUR-AANE MIN QABLE AN YYUQZAAA ELAYKA WAHYUH WA QUL RABBIL ZEDNEAA I’LMAN.\nHigh above all is Allah, the King, the Truth! Be not in haste with the Qur'an before its revelation to thee is completed, but say, “O my Lord! advance me in knowledge.” \nوَلَقَدْ عَهِدْنَاۤ اِلٰٓى اٰدَمَ مِنْ قَبْلُ فَنَسِىَ وَلَمْ نَجِدْ لَهٗ عَزْمًا‏(115)\nWA LAQAD A’AHEDNAA ELAA AADAMAL MIN QABLO FANASEAAA WA LAM NAJED LAHU A’AZMAN.\nWe had already, beforehand, taken the covenant of Adam, but he forgot: and We found on his part no firm resolve. \nوَاِذْ قُلْنَا لِلْمَلٰٓئِكَةِ اسْجُدُوْا لِاٰدَمَ فَسَجَدُوْۤا اِلَّاۤ اِبْلِيْسَؕ اَبٰى‏(116)\nWA IZ QULNAL LIL-MALAAA-EKATE JODOO LE-AADAMA FASAJADOOA ILLAA IBLEES ABAA.\nWhen We said to the angels, “Prostrate yourselves to Adam”, they prostrated themselves, but not Iblis: he refused. \nفَقُلْنَا يٰۤاٰدَمُ اِنَّ هٰذَا عَدُوٌّ لَّكَ وَلِزَوْجِكَ فَلَا يُخْرِجَنَّكُمَا مِنَ الْجَنَّةِ فَتَشْقٰى‏(117)\nFAQULNAA YAA AADAMO INNAL HAAZAA A’DUWWUM LAKA WALEZAWJEKA FALAA YUKHREJANNAKUMAA MENAL JANNAH FATASHQAA.\nThen We said: “O Adam! verily, this is an enemy to thee and thy wife: so let him not get you both out of the Garden, so that thou art landed in misery. \nاِنَّ لَكَ اَلَّا تَجُوْعَ فِيْهَا وَلَا تَعْرٰىۙ‏(118)\nINNAL LAKA ALLAA TAJOOA’A FEEHAA WA LAA TAA’RAA.\n“There is therein (enough provision) for thee not to go hungry nor to go naked, \nوَاَنَّكَ لَا تَظْمَؤُا فِيْهَا وَلَا تَضْحٰى‏(119)\nWA ANNAKA LAA TAZMAUA FEEHAA WA LAA TAZHAA.\n“Nor to suffer from thirst, nor from the sun's heat.” \nفَوَسْوَسَ اِلَيْهِ الشَّيْطٰنُ قَالَ يٰۤاٰدَمُ هَلْ اَدُلُّكَ عَلٰى شَجَرَةِ الْخُلْدِ وَمُلْكٍ لَّا يَبْلٰى‏(120)\nFAWASWASA ELAYHE SHAYTAANO QAALA YAA AADAMO HAL AADULLUKA A’LAA SHAJARATE AL-KHULDE WAMULKIN LAA YABLAA.\nBut Satan whispered evil to him: he said, “O Adam! shall I lead thee to the Tree of Eternity and to a kingdom that never decays?” \nفَاَكَلَا مِنْهَا فَبَدَتْ لَهُمَا سَوْاٰ تُہُمَا وَطَفِقَا يَخْصِفٰنِ عَلَيْهِمَا مِنْ وَّرَقِ الْجَنَّةِ‌ وَعَصٰۤى اٰدَمُ رَبَّهٗ فَغَوٰى‌ۖ‏(121)\nFAAKALAA MINHAA FABADAT LAHOMAA SAWAAA TUHUMAA WATAFEQAA YAKHSEFAANE FEEMAF MIN WWARAQE JANNAH WAA’ASAA AADAMO WAL FAGHAWAA.\nIn the result, they both ate of the tree, and so their nakedness appeared to them: they began to sew together, for their covering, leaves from the Garden: thus did Adam disobey his Lord, and allow himself to be seduced. \nثُمَّ اجْتَبٰهُ رَبُّهٗ فَتَابَ عَلَيْهِ وَهَدٰى‏(122)\nSUMMA AJTABAAHU RABBOHU FA-TAABA A’LAYHE WAHADAA.\nBut his Lord chose him (for His Grace): He turned to him, and gave him Guidance. \nقَالَ اهْبِطَا مِنْهَا جَمِيْعًا‌ۢ بَعْضُكُمْ لِبَعْضٍ عَدُوٌّ‌ ۚ فَاِمَّا يَاْتِيَنَّكُمْ مِّنِّىْ هُدًى ۙ فَمَنِ اتَّبَعَ هُدَاىَ فَلَا يَضِلُّ وَلَا يَشْقٰى‏(123)\nQAALA AHBETAA MINHAA JAMEE-A’A BA’ZOKUM LE-BA’ZIN A’DUWWUM FA-IMMAA YAATEYANNAKUM MINNEE HODAM FAMANE’ TABA-A’L HODAAYA FALAA YAZELLU WA LAA YASHQAA.\nHe said: “Get ye down, both of you, all together, from the Garden, with enmity one to another: but if, as is sure, there comes to you Guidance from Me, whosoever follows My Guidance, will not lose his way, nor fall into misery. \nوَمَنْ اَعْرَضَ عَنْ ذِكْرِىْ فَاِنَّ لَهٗ مَعِيْشَةً ضَنْكًا وَّنَحْشُرُهٗ يَوْمَ الْقِيٰمَةِ اَعْمٰى‏(124)\nWA MAN A-A’RAZA A’N ZEKREAA FA-INNAL LAHU MAE’EESHATAN ZANKAN WWANAHSHURUH YAWMA QEYAAMATE AAA’MAA.\n“But whosoever turns away from My Message, verily for him is a life narrowed down, and We shall raise him up blind on the Day of Judgment.” \nقَالَ رَبِّ لِمَ حَشَرْتَنِىْۤ اَعْمٰى وَقَدْ كُنْتُ بَصِيْرًا‏(125)\nQAALA RABBE LEMA HASHARTANEAA AAA’MAA WA QAD KUNTO BASEERAA.\nHe will say: “O my Lord! why hast Thou raised me up blind, while I had sight (before)?” \nقَالَ كَذٰلِكَ اَتَتْكَ اٰيٰتُنَا فَنَسِيْتَهَا‌ۚ وَكَذٰلِكَ الْيَوْمَ تُنْسٰى‏(126)\nQAALA KAZAALEKA AATATKA AAYAATONAA FANASEETAHAA WA KAZAALEKA YAWMA TUNSAA.\n(Allah) will say: “Thus didst Thou, when Our Signs came unto thee, disregard them: so wilt thou, this day, be disregarded.” \nوَكَذٰلِكَ نَجزِىْ مَنْ اَسْرَفَ وَلَمْ يُؤْمِنْۢ بِاٰيٰتِ رَبِّهٖ‌ؕ وَلَعَذَابُ الْاٰخِرَةِ اَشَدُّ وَاَبْقٰى‏(127)\nWA KAZAALEKA NAJZEAA MAN AASRAFA WA LAM YO’MIM BE-AAYAATIL RABBEH LA-A’ZAABUL AAKHERATE ASHADDO WAABQAA.\nAnd thus do We recompense him who transgresses beyond bounds and believes not in the Signs of his Lord: and the Penalty of the Hereafter is far more grievous and more enduring. \nاَفَلَمْ يَهْدِ لَهُمْ كَمْ اَهْلَكْنَا قَبْلَهُمْ مِّنَ الْقُرُوْنِ يَمْشُوْنَ فِىْ مَسٰكِنِهِمْ‌ؕ اِنَّ فِىْ ذٰ لِكَ لَاٰيٰتٍ لِّاُولِى النُّهٰى‏(128)\nA-FALAM YAHDE LAHUM KAM AHLAKNAL QABLAHUM MENAL QOROONE YAMSHOONA FEE MASAAKENEHEM INNAL FEE ZAA LEKA LA-AAYAATIL LEAOOLEAA AN-NUHAA.\nIs it not a warning to such men (to call to mind) how many generations before them We destroyed, in whose haunts they (now) move? Verily, in this are Signs for men endued with understanding. \nوَلَوْلَا كَلِمَةٌ سَبَقَتْ مِنْ رَّبِّكَ لَكَانَ لِزَامًا وَّاَجَلٌ مُّسَمًّىؕ‏(129)\nWA LAWLAA KALEMATUN SABAQAT MIN RABBEKA LAKAANA LEZAAMAN WWAAJALUN MOSAMMAA.\nHad it not been for a Word that went forth before from thy Lord, (their punishment) must necessarily have come; but there is a Term appointed (for respite). \nفَاصْبِرْ عَلٰى مَا يَقُوْلُوْنَ وَسَبِّحْ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّكَ قَبْلَ طُلُوْعِ الشَّمْسِ وَقَبْلَ غُرُوْبِهَا‌ ۚ وَمِنْ اٰنَآىٴِ الَّيْلِ فَسَبِّحْ وَاَطْرَافَ النَّهَارِ لَعَلَّكَ تَرْضٰى‏(130)\nFAS-BIR A’LAA MAA YAQOOLOONA WASABBEH BE-HAMDE RABBEKA QABLA TULOOE’E ASH-SHAMSE WA QABLA GHUROOBEHAA WA MIN AAANAAAAE LAYLE FA-SABBEH WAATRAAFA AN-NAHAARE LAA’ALLAKA TARZAA.\nTherefore be patient with what they say, and celebrate (constantly) the praises of thy Lord, before the rising of the sun, and before its setting; yea, celebrate them for part of the hours of the night, and at the sides of the day: that thou mayest have (spiritual) joy. \nوَلَا تَمُدَّنَّ عَيْنَيْكَ اِلٰى مَا مَتَّعْنَا بِهٖۤ اَزْوَاجًا مِّنْهُمْ زَهْرَةَ الْحَيٰوةِ الدُّنْيَا ۙ لِنَفْتِنَهُمْ فِيْهِ‌ ؕ وَرِزْقُ رَبِّكَ خَيْرٌ وَّاَبْقٰى‏(131)\nWA LAA TAMUDDANNA A’AYNAYKA ELAA MAA MATTAA’NAA BEHI AZWAAJANW MINHUM ZAHRATA HAYAATID DUNYAA LENAFTENAHUM FEEHE WAREZQU RABBEKA KHAYRUL KHAYRUWN.\nNor strain thine eyes in longing for the things We have given for enjoyment to parties of them, the splendour of the life of this world, through which We test them: but the provision of thy Lord is better and more enduring. \nوَاْمُرْ اَهْلَكَ بِالصَّلٰوةِ وَاصْطَبِرْ عَلَيْهَا‌ ؕ لَا نَسْئَلُكَ رِزْقًا‌ ؕ نَحْنُ نَرْزُقُكَ‌ ؕ وَالْعَاقِبَةُ لِلتَّقْوٰى‏(132)\nWAAMUR AHLAKA BEALSSALAAWTE WAASTABER A’LAYHAA LAA NASALUKA RIZQAN NAHNO NARZUQUKA A-A’QEBATO LELTTAQWAA.\nEnjoin prayer on thy people, and be constant therein. We ask thee not to provide sustenance: We provide it for thee. But the (fruit of) the Hereafter is for righteousness. \nوَقَالُوْا لَوْلَا يَاْتِيْنَا بِاٰيَةٍ مِّنْ رَّبِّهٖ ‌ؕ اَوَلَمْ تَاْتِہِمْ بَيِّنَةُ مَا فِى الصُّحُفِ الْاُوْلٰى‏(133)\nWA QAALOO LAWLAA YAATEENAA BE-AAYATIL MIN RABBEHI AWALAM TAATEHEM BAYNATU MAA FIL SOHOFIL OOLAA.\nThey say: “Why does he not bring us a sign from his Lord?” Has not a Clear Sign come to them of all that was in the former Books of revelation? \nوَلَوْ اَنَّاۤ اَهْلَكْنٰهُمْ بِعَذَابٍ مِّنْ قَبْلِهٖ لَقَالُوْا رَبَّنَا لَوْلَاۤ اَرْسَلْتَ اِلَيْنَا رَسُوْلًا فَنَتَّبِعَ اٰيٰتِكَ مِنْ قَبْلِ اَنْ نَّذِلَّ وَنَخْزٰى‏(134)\nWA LAW ANNAA AHLAKNAAHUM BE-A’ZAABIN MIN QABLEHI LAQAALOOA RABBANAA LAWLAA ARSALTA ELAYNAA RASOOLAM FANATTABE-A’ AAYAATEKA MIN QABLE AN NNAZELLA WANAKHZAA.\nAnd if We had inflicted on them a penalty before this, they would have said: “Our Lord! If only Thou hadst sent us a messenger, we should certainly have followed Thy Signs before we were humbled and put to shame.” \nقُلْ كُلٌّ مُّتَرَبِّصٌ فَتَرَبَّصُوْا‌ ۚ فَسَتَعْلَمُوْنَ مَنْ اَصْحٰبُ الصِّرَاطِ السَّوِىِّ وَمَنِ اهْتَدٰى‏(135)\nQUL KULLUL MMUTARABBESUN FATARABBASOOA FA-SATA’LAMOONA MAN ASHAABUN AS-SERAATE AS-SAWEAAAE MANIT TADAA.\nSay: “Each one (of us) is waiting: wait ye, therefore, and soon shall ye know who it is that is on the straight and even way, and who it is that has received Guidance.” ",
  "merits": "This Surah was revealed in Makkah and has 135 verses. It is mentioned in a narration from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that whoever recites this Surah will get the reward equivalent to the number of companions of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) from the Mohaajereen and Ansaar.\nImam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that Allah (s.w.t.) befriends the ones who recite this Surah and this person will receive his book of deeds on his right hand. His sins will be forgiven and he will get so much reward that he will be pleased on the Day of Judgement.\nThis Surah should be recited before war, going before a tyrant ruler and trying to guide a community towards the path of Allah (s.w.t.). If a girl is not getting married and she wishes to get married, she should take ghusl (bath) with water in which this Surah has been dissolved and by the will of Allah (s.w.t.) she will get married.\nIf a man wishes to get married, he should write verses 131 and 132 of this Surah with saffron and then wear it as a talisman and Inshallah his proposal will be accepted."
